    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-14T15:55:56+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T15:55:56+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-14T05:25:56Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-14T05:25:56Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure will establish over Western Australia and extend into the northwest of the state. A high pressure system moves southeast across waters to the south of SA, reaching the Tasman Sea later on Thursday and extends a ridge over the state until early next week. Another trough moves into the far west on Friday before weakening over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-14T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-14T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla early this evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla early this evening. Winds easterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the late afternoon and evening. Thunderstorms possibly severe with heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the far west in the late afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 31.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 31.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-18T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-17T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-18T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-17T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far west in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northeasterly during the morning then tending east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
